=== Stage 6: grounded, cited answer over the BM25-only fused set ===
Based on the retrieved context (doc_lineage_c00, doc_kafka_c01, doc_quality_c00):
OpenLineage emits START, COMPLETE, and FAIL run events for every pipeline stage. Each event carries a job name, a run id, and a producer URL, and is written as line-delimited JSON so lineage can be audited without a running Marquez server. It uses partitions and offsets to guarantee message ordering within a partition. In this capstone, Kafka is the ingestion boundary: every order event is published to the orders_raw topic before being validated against the OrderEventContract. Great Expectations validates the Silver orders table against six expectations covering completeness, uniqueness, and validity. A failed expectation raises QualityGateFailure, which the Airflow task re-raises so the DAG halts before Gold or RAG indexing runs.

[Sources: doc_lineage_c00, doc_kafka_c01, doc_quality_c00]

NOTE: this run exercises chunking + BM25 + RRF + citation end-to-end for real. The dense ChromaDB index and cross-encoder rerank need huggingface.co, unavailable in this build sandbox — run this file in Colab once (models auto-download on first call to build_vector_index/rerank) to capture the full hybrid+reranked output.
